# Developer Workspace

The selected direction is an explorer, continuous README canvas, sequential project
rows and optional profile/context rail. It is implemented with normal semantic HTML
and CSS. Consult the current `DESIGN.md` when present and preserve the approved
composition; a terminal or editor dependency is not needed for the visual identity.

`workspace.css` owns Tailwind v4, the two local font definitions and workspace
tokens; `reading.css` supplies the quieter technical-reading treatment. Geist Sans carries
headings and prose, Geist Mono labels/code. Fonts remain self-hosted in
`src/public/fonts/`. Newsreader definitions and serif-led legacy styles are retained
for the incumbent path, outside the Astro dependency graph.

System is the default theme in CSS: classless HTML follows the OS, `.light` and
`.dark` override. Keep the guarded pre-paint bootstrap and both dark palette blocks
consistent. Run `yarn check:contrast` after any palette edit; actual workspace,
reader and code-highlight colors need AA/sRGB verification, not visual estimates.

Desktop context is optional; at 900px and below navigation discloses and primary
content becomes one column. Preserve visible focus, native controls, meaningful
reading order, mobile contents, reduced motion and narrow reflow. Use existing
tokens and actual primitives rather than adding ornamental effects or a logo wall.
